  ('math.alg.ineq', 'math.alg.ineq.solve', 'easy', -1, 'mcq', null, 'Which inequality is equivalent to $4x - 1 < 3$?', '[{"id":"A","text":"$x > 1$"},{"id":"B","text":"$x \\le 1$"},{"id":"C","text":"$x < 1$"},{"id":"D","text":"$x < 4$"}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"C"}'::jsonb, 'Subtract -1: $4x < 4$. Divide by 4 (positive, so the sign stays): $x < 1$.', '{"A":"Reverses the inequality; dividing by a positive number keeps its direction.","B":"Includes the boundary, but the original inequality is strict.","D":"Forgets to divide by 4."}'::jsonb),
