  ('math.geo.trig', 'math.geo.trig.pythagorean', 'medium', 0, 'mcq', null, 'In a 30°-60°-90° triangle, the side opposite the 30° angle has length 11. What is the length of the side opposite the 60° angle?', '[{"id":"A","text":"$22$"},{"id":"B","text":"$11\\sqrt{3}$"},{"id":"C","text":"$11\\sqrt{2}$"},{"id":"D","text":"$22\\sqrt{3}$"}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"B"}'::jsonb, 'The sides of a 30°-60°-90° triangle are in the ratio $1 : \sqrt{3} : 2$. The side opposite 60° is $\sqrt{3}$ times the shortest side: $11\sqrt{3}$.', '{"A":"This is the hypotenuse, not the longer leg.","C":"Uses the 45°-45°-90° ratio.","D":"Doubles the longer leg."}'::jsonb),
