  ('math.psda.inference', 'math.psda.inference.moe', 'hard', 1, 'mcq', null, 'Two researchers each select a random sample of residents from the same city to estimate the percentage who use a recycling program. One samples 150 residents and the other samples 450 residents. Which statement is most likely true?', '[{"id":"A","text":"The survey of 150 residents is likely to have a smaller margin of error."},{"id":"B","text":"Both surveys will have the same margin of error because they use the same method."},{"id":"C","text":"The survey of 450 residents is likely to have a smaller margin of error."},{"id":"D","text":"The survey of 450 residents will give exactly the true percentage."}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"C"}'::jsonb, 'With the same sampling method, a larger random sample gives a more precise estimate, so its margin of error is smaller.', '{"A":"Smaller samples have larger margins of error.","B":"The margin of error depends on sample size.","D":"A larger sample reduces error but never removes it."}'::jsonb),
