  ('math.psda.claims', 'math.psda.claims.design', 'medium', 0, 'mcq', null, 'Researchers recruited seedlings from one greenhouse and randomly assigned half to use a new fertilizer and half not to. The group using a new fertilizer showed significantly better plant height. Which conclusion is best supported?', '[{"id":"A","text":"A new fertilizer likely causes improved plant height for seedlings from one greenhouse."},{"id":"B","text":"A new fertilizer causes improved plant height for everyone."},{"id":"C","text":"There is an association, but no conclusion about cause can be drawn."},{"id":"D","text":"No conclusion can be drawn because the groups were chosen at random."}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Random assignment supports a cause-and-effect conclusion, but because the participants were not randomly selected from a larger population, the conclusion applies only to people like the participants.', '{"B":"The participants were not a random sample of everyone.","C":"Random assignment to groups is what allows a cause-and-effect conclusion.","D":"Random assignment strengthens, not weakens, the conclusion."}'::jsonb),
