  ('math.psda.claims', 'math.psda.claims.design', 'hard', 1, 'mcq', null, 'An observational study of a large random sample of adults found that those who drink more coffee were more likely to sleep fewer hours. Participants chose their own habits; none were assigned. Which statement is best supported?', '[{"id":"A","text":"People who drink more coffee tend to sleep fewer hours, but the study does not show that one causes the other."},{"id":"B","text":"Choosing to drink more coffee causes people to sleep fewer hours."},{"id":"C","text":"There is no relationship between whether people drink more coffee and whether they sleep fewer hours."},{"id":"D","text":"Everyone who chose to drink more coffee will sleep fewer hours."}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"A"}'::jsonb, 'A random sample supports generalizing the association to the population, but because habits were not randomly assigned, the study cannot show cause and effect.', '{"B":"Without random assignment, other factors could explain the link.","C":"The study did find an association.","D":"An association describes a tendency, not a certainty for every person."}'::jsonb),
