  ('math.geo.area', 'math.geo.area.volume', 'hard', 1, 'mcq', null, 'Every linear dimension of a rectangular prism is multiplied by 4. The surface area of the new rectangular prism is how many times the surface area of the original?', '[{"id":"A","text":"$16$"},{"id":"B","text":"$4$"},{"id":"C","text":"$64$"},{"id":"D","text":"$12$"}]'::jsonb, '{"choice":"A"}'::jsonb, 'Surface area scales by the square of the scale factor: $4^{2} = 16$.', '{"B":"Scales by k only once; each dimension contributes a factor.","C":"Surface area uses two dimensions, so the factor is squared.","D":"Adds the factor three times instead of multiplying."}'::jsonb),
